Run be-csharp's async steps one at a time on one thread, and hold top-level code in a turn.
Upstream: not yet; to offer Kotlin Temper (its issue 516, which PR #532 leaves for C#).

Blocks started with `Task.Run` and resumed by `ContinueWith` ran in
parallel. Now every step goes on one FIFO drained by a `temper-async`
thread, under a turn lock that the library template's `Main` holds
around top-level code (`BeginTopLevel`, `EndTopLevel`), so a settled
task only queues its waiter.

